{
  "alias": "pf-agentic-identity",
  "description": "PingFederate 13.1.3 + pf-agentic-identity modules. FAPI 2.0 Security Profile Final: client_attestation (attest_jwt_client_auth, the suite as attester), DPoP, plain_fapi, OpenID Connect. Needs a suite that offers client_attestation with plain_fapi, and the rig's fapi2-attestation profile.",
  "server": {
    "discoveryUrl": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/.well-known/openid-configuration"
  },
  "client": {
    "client_id": "conformance-fapi2-attest-client1",
    "scope": "openid profile",
    "jwks": "{{JWKS:fapi2-client1}}"
  },
  "client2": {
    "client_id": "conformance-fapi2-attest-client2",
    "scope": "openid profile",
    "jwks": "{{JWKS:fapi2-client2}}"
  },
  "client_attestation": {
    "comment": "The suite mints each Client Attestation JWT (sub = the client id, cnf = a client instance key it generates) and signs it with attester_jwks, whose key carries x5c. PingFederate trusts this attester's public key directly (oidf.mock.attesters) and binds both clients to it (OIDF_BRIDGE_SIGNING_KEYS). The clients' own jwks are the FAPI 2.0 clients' keys, which the suite insists on having; nothing authenticates with them here.",
    "issuer": "https://suite-attester.rig.example",
    "attester_jwks": "{{JWKS:suite-attester}}"
  },
  "resource": {
    "resourceUrl": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/idp/userinfo.openid"
  },
  "browser": [
    {
      "comment": "PingFederate's stock HTML form, then its stock consent page, then the suite's own callback. Selectors are the ids in html.form.login.template.html and oauth.approval.page.template.html.",
      "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
      "tasks": [
        {
          "task": "Sign in",
          "optional": true,
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
          "commands": [
            [
              "text",
              "id",
              "username",
              "suite-user"
            ],
            [
              "text",
              "id",
              "password",
              "{{TEST_USER_PASSWORD}}"
            ],
            [
              "click",
              "id",
              "signOnButton"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "task": "Consent",
          "optional": true,
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/*/resume/as/authorization.ping*",
          "commands": [
            [
              "click",
              "id",
              "allowButton"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "task": "Back at the suite",
          "match": "*/test/a/*/callback*",
          "commands": [
            [
              "wait",
              "id",
              "submission_complete",
              10
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "override": {
    "fapi2-security-profile-final-user-rejects-authentication": {
      "browser": [
        {
          "comment": "The one module where the user says no. Same sign-in, then Don't Allow; PingFederate answers the client with error=access_denied.",
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
          "tasks": [
            {
              "task": "Sign in",
              "optional": true,
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "text",
                  "id",
                  "username",
                  "suite-user"
                ],
                [
                  "text",
                  "id",
                  "password",
                  "{{TEST_USER_PASSWORD}}"
                ],
                [
                  "click",
                  "id",
                  "signOnButton"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "Refuse consent",
              "optional": true,
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/*/resume/as/authorization.ping*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "click",
                  "id",
                  "denyButton"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "Back at the suite",
              "match": "*/test/a/*/callback*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "wait",
                  "id",
                  "submission_complete",
                  10
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "fapi2-security-profile-final-par-attempt-reuse-request_uri": {
      "browser": [
        {
          "comment": "First use of the request_uri: an ordinary sign-in.",
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
          "match-limit": 1,
          "tasks": [
            {
              "task": "Sign in",
              "optional": true,
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "text",
                  "id",
                  "username",
                  "suite-user"
                ],
                [
                  "text",
                  "id",
                  "password",
                  "{{TEST_USER_PASSWORD}}"
                ],
                [
                  "click",
                  "id",
                  "signOnButton"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "Consent",
              "optional": true,
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/*/resume/as/authorization.ping*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "click",
                  "id",
                  "allowButton"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "Back at the suite",
              "match": "*/test/a/*/callback*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "wait",
                  "id",
                  "submission_complete",
                  10
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "comment": "Second use of the same request_uri: 400 invalid_request_uri.",
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
          "tasks": [
            {
              "task": "PingFederate refuses the request_uri",
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "wait",
                  "xpath",
                  "//*",
                  10,
                  "invalid_request_uri",
                  "update-image-placeholder"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "fapi2-security-profile-final-par-attempt-to-use-expired-request_uri": {
      "browser": [
        {
          "comment": "The suite waited out expires_in before coming here: 400 invalid_request_uri.",
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
          "tasks": [
            {
              "task": "PingFederate refuses the request_uri",
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "wait",
                  "xpath",
                  "//*",
                  10,
                  "invalid_request_uri",
                  "update-image-placeholder"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "fapi2-security-profile-final-par-attempt-to-use-request_uri-for-different-client": {
      "browser": [
        {
          "comment": "Client 2 presenting client 1's request_uri: 400 invalid_request_uri, Client mismatch.",
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
          "tasks": [
            {
              "task": "PingFederate refuses the request_uri",
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "wait",
                  "xpath",
                  "//*",
                  10,
                  "invalid_request_uri",
                  "update-image-placeholder"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "fapi2-security-profile-final-par-ensure-reused-request-uri-prior-to-auth-completion-succeeds": {
      "browser": [
        {
          "comment": "First visit: reach the sign-in page and stop. The module fails if anyone signs in before the second visit.",
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
          "match-limit": 1,
          "tasks": [
            {
              "task": "Look at the sign-in page, and leave",
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "wait",
                  "id",
                  "username",
                  10
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "comment": "Second visit, same request_uri, nobody has signed in yet. PingFederate 13.1.3 shows the sign-in page: it spends a request_uri at the point of authorization, as FAPI 2.0 Final 5.3.2.2 NOTE 3 recommends, so the module can PASS. (13.0.3 spent it when the page was LOADED and answered invalid_request_uri here; that version of this entry waited for the error page and the module ended in REVIEW.)",
          "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
          "tasks": [
            {
              "task": "Sign in",
              "optional": true,
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/authorization.oauth2*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "text",
                  "id",
                  "username",
                  "suite-user"
                ],
                [
                  "text",
                  "id",
                  "password",
                  "{{TEST_USER_PASSWORD}}"
                ],
                [
                  "click",
                  "id",
                  "signOnButton"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "Consent",
              "optional": true,
              "match": "{{PF_BASE_URL}}/as/*/resume/as/authorization.ping*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "click",
                  "id",
                  "allowButton"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "Back at the suite",
              "match": "*/test/a/*/callback*",
              "commands": [
                [
                  "wait",
                  "id",
                  "submission_complete",
                  10
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
